 "short_name": "Setsoto",
 "_doc": "Emunsoft statement in two variants: 8 bills as the standard layout, 2 'REPRINT' bills with LEVIED AMOUNT / READING DATES (start - end), '@'/'*' markers, an undated TOTAL PAYMENTS line and a scrambled street cell. Fingerprint: Setsoto's own VAT number + 'SETSOTO MUNICIPALITY'. Both energy and demand lines print as 'ELECTRICITY'; they are told apart by the tariff column (R/kWh below 100 = energy -> standard, R/kVA of 100+ = demand). BASIC ELECTRICITY -> other. An undated INTEREST line follows the VAT line on most bills. IDENTITY x_elec_resid_r = TOTAL DUE - Opening Balance - TOTAL PAYMENTS - every non-electricity ledger line (payments, other services, interest, rebates) - the VAT line - undated INTEREST, i.e. the electricity total implied by the bill's own balance movement, independent of the electricity lines; 0.00 gap on all 10 bills (10 checked).",
 "fingerprint": {
